  "body": "### Summary\nAs the maintainer, I want an independent performance review of SwiftHFR by **Fable 5.2** (or the latest Fable at the time) at the end of M4, so that every slow path, blocked main thread, wasted computation and slow answer is found, measured and turned into an actionable issue before release. Operator request, 2026-11-10.\n\n### On hold\n\nHeld by the operator's schedule (request of 2026-11-10, this issue's \"When\"): the review starts when the M4 lots are merged; the orchestrator starts it. ([decision](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/issues/774))\n\n\n### When\nEnd of M4, **first** of two sequential reviews; review 2/2 (reliability and maintainability) starts only after this one is closed. `status: blocked` until the M4 lots are merged (the orchestrator unblocks it).\n\n### Scope\nApp (`App/SwiftHFR`) and engine (`Packages/HFRKit`): launch time, list and reader scrolling (hitches), time to first message (#750), main-actor work, parsing and normalization cost (LESSONS 4, 49), network round trips and redirects, image and web-view loading, caching, memory and energy, background work (MP poll, sync), responsiveness of every user action (tap to visible result).\n\n### Method\n- Measure, never assume (AGENTS §3 rule 9): Instruments (Time Profiler, Hangs, Animation Hitches, Network, Allocations, Energy) on a **device** and on the simulator, the same scenarios on legacy for comparison; numbers before and after.\n- Read the code paths behind each hot spot; check algorithmic complexity on large inputs (long topics, deep quotes, big lists).\n- The reviewer is independent of the authors (AGENTS §6): it gets the code and the measurements, not the authors' conclusions.\n\n### Output\n- One comment on this issue: the measured baseline (table per scenario, device and build), the ranked list of findings.\n- **One issue per finding**, each with: `### Summary` (intent, user story), the measurement and the code to review (`file:line`), the test that proves it (a performance test or a measured threshold, failing before the fix), the definition of done, and the **ideal model for the rework** (AGENTS §6 routing), with labels on every axis.\n- No code change in this issue.\n\n### Definition of done\n- [ ] Baseline measured on device and simulator, legacy compared.\n- [ ] Every finding filed as an issue as above; this issue closed with the list.\n\nRefs #750, #704, #772.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
